# Leo MVP - Walkthrough

**Leo** is your Telegram-based second brain—a system to instantly capture text and links via Telegram and retrieve them later through a searchable web inbox.

## 🚀 Usage Guide

### 1. Capture (Telegram)
- **Bot:** [@muntaleobot](https://t.me/muntaleobot)
- **Text:** Send any message to save it instantly.
- **URLs:** Send links; Leo automatically detects them.
- **Confirmation:** Wait for the "Saved ✅" reply.
- **Failures:** If saving fails, you'll see a "❌ Failed to save" message (rare).

### 2. Retrieval (Web Inbox)
- **URL:** https://leo-brain.vercel.app
- **Login:** Enter password `LeoSecure2026!`
- **Inbox:** View all your saved items, grouped by date (Today, Yesterday, This Week, etc.).
- **URL Handling:** Links are clickable and open in a new tab.

### 3. Actions
- **Copy:** Click the clipboard icon to copy content to your clipboard.
- **Archive:** Click the file box icon to move items to the archive. They are hidden from the inbox but not deleted.
- **View Archive:** Link in the footer takes you to archived items.

### 4. Search
- **Input:** Type in the search bar at the top of the inbox.
- **Filter:** Results update in real-time as you type.
- **Scope:** Search covers both text content and URLs.
- **Clear:** Click the 'X' to reset the view.

---

## 🛠️ Technical Overview

### 1. Stack
- **Frontend:** Next.js 14 (App Router), TypeScript, Tailwind CSS
- **Database:** Neon PostgreSQL (Serverless)
- **ORM:** Drizzle ORM
- **Deployment:** Vercel

### 2. Key Features
- **Telegram Webhook:** Real-time message processing with rate limiting (10 msg/sec).
- **Reliability:** 1 retry on database failures, structured logging for debugging.
- **Authentication:** Password protection with HTTP-only cookies and JWT (Jose).
- **Search:** Case-insensitive PostgreSQL ILIKE search with debouncing.
- **Rate Limiting:** In-memory rate limiter to prevent abuse.

### 3. Project Structure
- [src/app/api/telegram/webhook/route.ts](file:///Users/maruthi/Desktop/MainDirectory/Leo/src/app/api/telegram/webhook/route.ts): Main entry point for Telegram messages.
- [src/lib/db/schema.ts](file:///Users/maruthi/Desktop/MainDirectory/Leo/src/lib/db/schema.ts): Database schema definition.
- [src/lib/auth.ts](file:///Users/maruthi/Desktop/MainDirectory/Leo/src/lib/auth.ts): Authentication logic (Session management).
- [src/lib/logger.ts](file:///Users/maruthi/Desktop/MainDirectory/Leo/src/lib/logger.ts): Structured logging utility.
- [src/components/ItemCard.tsx](file:///Users/maruthi/Desktop/MainDirectory/Leo/src/components/ItemCard.tsx): UI component for inbox items using Glassmorphism design.

---

## 🔒 Security
- **Environment Variables:** All secrets (`DATABASE_URL`, `TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN`, `ADMIN_PASSWORD`, `SESSION_SECRET`) are stored in Vercel environment variables and encrypted.
- **Auth:** Session tokens are signed/verified using `jose` and stored in secure, HTTP-only cookies.
- **Middleware:** Next.js middleware protects `/inbox` and `/archive` routes.

---

## 🔮 Future Enhancements (Post-MVP)
- **File Support:** Upload images and PDFs (Schema already supports this).
- **Smart Search:** Vector embeddings for semantic search.
- **User Accounts:** Multi-user support with individual logins.
- **Export:** Export data to JSON/CSV.
